{"title": "Brain Mapping Puzzle", "pageid": 36578, "url": "https://bg3.wiki/wiki/Brain_Mapping_Puzzle", "categories": ["Locations", "Act Two Locations"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>In the southeast section of the Necrotic Lab area of the <a href=\"/wiki/Mind_Flayer_Colony\" title=\"Mind Flayer Colony\">Mind Flayer Colony</a>, there is a console. Interacting with the console using Illithid powers projects an empty neural map of one of the brains the <a href=\"/wiki/Mind_flayers\" title=\"Mind flayers\">Mind Flayers</a> have been experimenting on. The neural map is basically a connect the dots puzzle; solving it allows to access the <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-common\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Waking_Mind\" title=\"Waking Mind\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/b/bf/Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/b/bf/Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/b/bf/Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png/40px-Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/b/bf/Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/b/bf/Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Waking_Mind\" title=\"Waking Mind\">Waking Mind</a>, which can be inserted into The Mind-Archive Interface at <span class=\"bg3wiki-coordinates\">X:&nbsp;699&nbsp;Y:&nbsp;-117</span> in order to gain the permanent buff: <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Githzerai_Mind_Barrier_(Condition)\" title=\"Githzerai Mind Barrier (Condition)\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/9/94/Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp/25px-Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/9/94/Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp/38px-Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/9/94/Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp/50px-Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Githzerai Mind Barrier\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/9/94/Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp/25px-Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/9/94/Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Githzerai_Mind_Barrier_(Condition)\" title=\"Githzerai Mind Barrier (Condition)\">Githzerai Mind Barrier</a>.\n</p><p>Solving the puzzle also grants the inspiration <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Sage#Brain_Blast!\" title=\"Sage\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/8/85/Inspiration_Icon.png/25px-Inspiration_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/8/85/Inspiration_Icon.png/38px-Inspiration_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/8/85/Inspiration_Icon.png/50px-Inspiration_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Brain Blast!\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/8/85/Inspiration_Icon.png/25px-Inspiration_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/8/85/Inspiration_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span>⁠<a href=\"/wiki/Sage#Brain_Blast!\" title=\"Sage\">Brain Blast!</a> for party members with the <a href=\"/wiki/Sage\" title=\"Sage\">Sage</a> background.\n</p><p><i><b>Note for console users</b></i>: To use the nodes, console users should enter interaction mode (L3; pressing down on the toggle stick) and select \"use\" on each node.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Puzzle_Solution\">Puzzle Solution</span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Brain_puzzle_solution.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/9/96/Brain_puzzle_solution.png/300px-Brain_puzzle_solution.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/9/96/Brain_puzzle_solution.png/450px-Brain_puzzle_solution.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/9/96/Brain_puzzle_solution.png/600px-Brain_puzzle_solution.png.webp 2x\"><img src=\"/w/images/thumb/9/96/Brain_puzzle_solution.png/300px-Brain_puzzle_solution.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"169\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/9/96/Brain_puzzle_solution.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a><figcaption>solution from left to right (Credit: Larian)</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Solving the puzzle requires to connect the four colored centers of the brain: <b>Speech</b>, <b>Emotion</b>, <b>Memory</b>, and <b>Reason</b>, to corresponding spots on the opposite side of the web of Neural Nodes. It is necessary to begin by selecting one of the four centers, then select each of the nodes that should be connected to it until a linked path is created, which reaches the corresponding center on the opposite side. <b>Note</b>: each brain center has its own individual path to the other side. The paths weave in between each other, but never use the same node. It does not matter which order the paths are charted in, as long as they are done one by one. \n</p><p>Once solved, a near door open to an area containing the <span class=\"nowrap bg3wiki-icontext-icon\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-itemicon bg3wiki-itemicon-common\"><span class=\"bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Waking_Mind\" title=\"Waking Mind\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/b/bf/Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp, /w/images/thumb/b/bf/Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png/30px-Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/b/bf/Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png/40px-Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/b/bf/Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png/20px-Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/b/bf/Brain_Jar_Memory_A_Unfaded_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Waking_Mind\" title=\"Waking Mind\">Waking Mind</a>. \n</p><p>Inserting the Waking Mind into the Mind-Archive Interface prompts a dialogue with the mind of a Githzerai who asks to purge their brain in exchange for their knowledge. Warlocks get an additional dialogue where they sense their Patron warning against trusting the Githzerai, allowing them to question the mind further about the circumstances leading up to their imprisonment in the Mind Flayer Colony. If choosing to purge their mind, the interacting party member gains the <span class=\"bg3wiki-icontext-icon nowrap\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/Githzerai_Mind_Barrier_(Condition)\" title=\"Githzerai Mind Barrier (Condition)\"><picture><source srcset=\"/w/images/thumb/9/94/Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp/25px-Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp, /w/images/thumb/9/94/Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp/38px-Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp 1.5x, /w/images/thumb/9/94/Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp/50px-Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp 2x\"><img alt=\"Githzerai Mind Barrier\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/9/94/Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp/25px-Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></a><a href=\"/w/images/9/94/Generic_Buff_Condition_Icon.webp\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> <a href=\"/wiki/Githzerai_Mind_Barrier_(Condition)\" title=\"Githzerai Mind Barrier (Condition)\">Githzerai Mind Barrier</a> condition, which gives advantage on all <a href=\"/wiki/Intelligence\" title=\"Intelligence\">intelligence</a> saving throws.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notes\">Notes</span></h2>\n<div class=\"notebegin\">\n<ul><li>The voice lines that play out when paths are completed are voiced by <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.imdb.com/name/nm14667542\">Grace Haydn</a>.</li></ul>\n</div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260714201657\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.046 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1982/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 11247/4194304 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 2423/4194304 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 19/200\nExpensive parser function count: 0/750\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 0/1000\nLua time usage: 0.015/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 812248/52428800 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   38.394      1 -total\n 53.02%   20.357      2 Template:SmRarityItem\n 33.53%   12.875      2 Template:Item_icon\n 27.67%   10.622      2 Template:Cond\n 13.95%    5.357     23 Template:Trim\n 13.78%    5.290      3 Template:Icon_link\n 12.24%    4.699      3 Template:Icon_text\n 11.79%    4.528      2 Template:Condition_inline/format\n 10.57%    4.059      4 Template:ItemIcon_Internal\n 10.41%    3.998      1 Template:Inspiration\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key bg3wiki:pcache:idhash:36578-0!canonical and timestamp 20260714201657 and revision id 397118. Rendering was triggered because: unknown\n -->\n</div>"}